Package: pubmaps
Title: Study-Site Maps for Journal Editors
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Kim", "Bridges", email = "kim.bridges@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Claude", role = "aut", comment = "Anthropic; collaborative development"),
    person("Will", "McClatchey", role = "ctb", comment = "editorial practice that shaped the tool"))
Description: Turns a manuscript into a publication-ready study-site map with a
    locator inset. A language model reads the manuscript and lists every
    mappable place with the page and sentence that mention it; the GeoNames and
    OpenStreetMap (Nominatim) gazetteers locate them, each position recorded with
    its source and match quality; fixed rules choose the projection, frame,
    inset, scale bar and north arrow, and draw parks and districts as areas
    and named rivers as lines. The
    editor checks everything on an HTML review page, corrects one table
    ('points.csv'), and redraws. Companion to the book 'PubMaps: Study-site maps
    for journal editors'.
